{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The Festival of Unleavened Bread you shall observe.</b> The reason for this commandment here is as an admonition, for these are the rectifications of the earlier sin, as they said, of blessed memory (Zohar 2:3a), that leaven is the aspect of 'another El'; therefore HaShem commanded with extra emphasis to observe this matter, and He commanded here concerning the totality of the festivals. Or perhaps it is because, since it was said concerning the calf (Exodus 32:4): ״אֵלֶּה אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר הֶעֱלוּךָ״ and so forth, and all the festivals depend on the Exodus from Egypt, therefore HaShem revisited the matter so that they would take upon themselves the particulars that have opposition to them implied by the statement of heresy — and this is one of the particulars of repentance that are necessary. And He mentioned the observance of Shabbat because they had committed idolatry, which is weighted equally against the entire Torah; therefore HaShem stated the commandment of Shabbat, which is likewise weighted equally against the entire Torah, for through this the distortion is rectified. And see what I wrote at the beginning of parashat Vayakhel."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:36.765152785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}